          "basis": "derived",
          "rationale": "The metres are Wilcox's own — 20 feet long, 15 to 16 wide, 4 high, aluminium coloured — and everything else here follows from them and from the angles the recording already states. Six point one metres seen across 19.22° puts the craft 18.1 m away, and 18.1 m due south of where he started is 3.3 m from where he stops walking, which is the \"close enough to touch\" of the account: the walk itself is what the file's own observer track says, so the distance is not a new claim but his figure read through his angles. That the long axis lies across his line of sight is read off the drawing, whose 19.22 by 3.82 degrees are in the ratio 5.0 of 20 feet to 4. On the ground it is his word; where exactly it rests on the relief is the relief's. The climb keeps his angles and takes its distance the same way, from the same 6.1 m, which is why the craft ends 264 m off: nobody measured that, the size did."
        }
